# Copy to .env and set the three values below. Nothing else is required.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose up -d --build
#   docker compose exec classifier python -m rag ingest --reset
#
# Full setup: README.md. Ollama backend: README.md section 4b.

# --- 1. Your chat model's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, AS SEEN FROM A CONTAINER
# Another box:            http://<its-ip>:4000/v1   (Ollama: :11434)
# Same host:              http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1
#   ^ works ONLY if that server is bound to 0.0.0.0 / the bridge IP, not
#   127.0.0.1. A 127.0.0.1-only server is unreachable from a container: bind it
#   to the docker bridge IP (README section 4a). A wrong value here sends every
#   email to the human queue, silently.
LLM_URL=http://host.docker.internal:4000/v1

# --- 2. API key (blank for Ollama, or a LiteLLM proxy with no auth) ----------
LLM_KEY=

# --- 3. The model name the endpoint exposes for chat ------------------------
# Used for BOTH classification and reply drafting. Point it at a capable
# instruction model you already run -- this project needs no model of its own.
#   LiteLLM: the model_list name        e.g. qwen3-27b
#   Ollama:  the pulled tag             e.g. qwen3:32b   (run `ollama list`)
CHAT_MODEL=qwen3-27b

# ===========================================================================
# OLLAMA BACKEND -- uncomment if CHAT_MODEL is served by Ollama.
# ===========================================================================
# Ollama's OpenAI endpoint returned no token logprobs before ~v0.12. Without
# them the classifier cannot compute confidence and sends EVERY email to the
# human queue. This routes on the model's bare true/false answer instead: still
# fails safe, but the confidence threshold no longer applies. Run the logprobs
# check in README.md section 4c first -- only set this if it comes back empty.
# EC_ALLOW_UNCALIBRATED=1
#
# Ollama defaults to a 4096-token context and silently truncates longer
# prompts, cutting off document extracts. Prefer OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192 on
# the Ollama service itself; this is the fallback if you cannot set that.
# EC_NUM_CTX=8192

# --- other optional settings ------------------------------------------------
# A larger model for `python -m rag ask --large` evals only. Defaults to CHAT_MODEL.
# CHAT_MODEL_LARGE=
# Classifier confidence bar for routing to the RAG auto-reply (default 0.9).
# EC_THRESHOLD=0.9
# P(non_academic) at which an email goes to a person (default: EC_THRESHOLD).
# EC_NON_ACADEMIC_THRESHOLD=0.9
# Reply-shell wording. A literal \n becomes a line break.
# RAG_EMAIL_GREETING=Hello,
# RAG_EMAIL_SIGNOFF=Best regards,\nThe Training Team

# ===========================================================================
# REVIEW QUEUE SEND (Graph) -- required only to make the Send button in
# /review actually deliver mail. Without these, the review queue still works
# for reading and editing drafts, but Send returns a 503 explaining what's
# missing rather than pretending to have sent anything.
#
# This is a SEPARATE, app-only Azure AD app registration from the Outlook
# OAuth2 credential the n8n workflow uses (that one is delegated -- it needs
# an interactive sign-in and is not what this reads). To create it:
#   1. Entra admin center -> App registrations -> New registration.
#   2. API permissions -> Microsoft Graph -> Application permissions -> add
#      Mail.Send -> Grant admin consent (a tenant admin must click this).
#   3. Certificates & secrets -> New client secret -> copy the VALUE, not the id.
#   4. Set the four values below from that app's Overview page and the
#      mailbox you want replies sent from.
# ===========================================================================
# GRAPH_TENANT_ID=
# GRAPH_CLIENT_ID=
# GRAPH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The mailbox to send as -- its UPN (usually the sign-in email), not a
# display name. App-only Graph calls address /users/{mailbox}/..., so this
# must be set even when it matches the inbox New Outlook email polls.
# GRAPH_MAILBOX=
#
# Testing the review queue's UI/DB flow (edit, Send, row disappears) without
# GRAPH_* set up yet, and without sending real mail while you do: set this to
# 1. Send then records the row as sent and skips the Graph call entirely.
# Unset or 0 for real use -- leave it off once you're done testing.
# REVIEW_DRY_RUN=1
